# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Intellij
# Covers JetBrains IDEs: IntelliJ, RubyMine, PhpStorm, AppCode, PyCharm, CLion, Android Studio and Webstorm
# Reference: https://intellij-support.jetbrains.com/hc/en-us/articles/206544839

# User-specific stuff:
.idea/**/workspace.xml
.idea/**/tasks.xml
.idea/dictionaries
.idea
.vscode

# Sensitive or high-churn files:
.idea/**/dataSources/
.idea/**/dataSources.ids
.idea/**/dataSources.xml
.idea/**/dataSources.local.xml
.idea/**/sqlDataSources.xml
.idea/**/dynamic.xml
.idea/**/uiDesigner.xml

# macOS
*.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Cached authenticated browser sessions written by e2e configs that log in
# once per run (Playwright storage state); may contain live auth tokens.
web/app/e2e/.auth/

# Lambda build artifacts
bootstrap

# Compiled binaries from cmd/. `go build ./cmd/<name>` drops the executable in
# the directory it is run from, so these land at the repo root named after the
# package — a 39MB platform-specific artifact that is rebuildable from source
# and has no business in git history. Listed explicitly rather than by glob: a
# bare `create-superuser` pattern would also ignore a future directory of that
# name, and the set of binaries is small enough to enumerate.
/create-superuser
/api-server
/generate-test-conversations

# Local dev background API artifacts (make dev-up)
.dev/
lambda.zip

# Grounding data
grounding-data/

# Compiled output
/dist
/tmp
/out-tsc
/bazel-out

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# IDEs and editors
.idea/
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace
.gomodcache/

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/*

# Miscellaneous
/.angular/cache
.sass-cache/
/connect.lock
/coverage
/libpeerconnection.log
testem.log
/typings

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Web - Build artifacts
web/*/node_modules/
web/*/dist/
web/*/.angular/
web/**/dist/
web/**/.angular/

# Web - Playwright E2E artifacts
web/**/test-results/
web/**/playwright-report/
web/**/playwright/.cache/
# Raw V8 coverage and the merged lcov/HTML from E2E_COVERAGE=1 runs. The root
# /coverage rule above is anchored to the repo root and does not reach these.
# Single-star on purpose: `web/**/coverage/` would also swallow the pipeline's
# own specs in `e2e/tests/functional/coverage/`.
web/*/coverage/
web/*/webcov/

# Terraform
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
*.tfvars.local
terraform.tfvars.local
crash.log
crash.*.log

# AI working files (private workspace for session continuity)
.ghost/
.claude/*
# ...but track shared, versioned Claude Code skills
!.claude/skills/
# ...except per-bug collected artifacts (local scratch, never committed)
.claude/skills/file-bug/artifacts/
.cursor/*
# ...but track shared, versioned Cursor agent rules (AGENTS.md points at these)
!.cursor/rules/
# ...and the project-scoped Playwright MCP definition.
!.cursor/mcp.json

# Large binaries and toolchains (should not be committed)
/stripe
stripe_*.tar.gz
go*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz

mockups/

# Local conversation export samples used for import testing (personal data — never commit)
docs/conversations.json
testdata/chat-import/large-conversations.json
# Derived at build time by web/app/scripts/write-version.mjs
web/app/public/version.json

# Ent generated code — produced by `go generate ./ent` (the Makefile `generate`
# target, run in CI and the Dockerfile before every build). The schema under
# ent/schema is the source of truth and IS tracked; the generated output is not
# checked in. Run `make generate` (or `make build`/`make test`, which depend on
# it) after cloning or changing a schema.
/ent/*
!/ent/schema
!/ent/generate.go
